[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Public entry points (the FULL set)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `nm -D` on the C `.so` lists exactly one exported function, and `lib.h` declares
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m exactly one prototype:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | entry point | signature | exported? |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|---|---|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `tritanopia` | `cb_rgb_255 tritanopia(cb_rgb_255 RGB)` | **yes** |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `cbNorm` | `static cb_rgb cbNorm(cb_rgb_255)` | no — `static`, absent from `nm -D` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `cbRemoveGammaRGB` | `static cb_rgb cbRemoveGammaRGB(cb_rgb)` | no — `static` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `Tritanopia` | `static void Tritanopia(float*, float*, float*)` | no — `static` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `cbApplyGammaRGB` | `static cb_rgb cbApplyGammaRGB(cb_rgb)` | no — `static` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `cbDenorm` | `static cb_rgb_255 cbDenorm(cb_rgb)` | no — `static` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The five lowest-level stages are `static` in the C, so they are **not reachable
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m through either `.so`** and cannot be called differentially without adding
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m exports the C `.so` does not have (which would break the Phase D symbol diff).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m They are instead driven *indirectly but exhaustively*: the rows below pin each
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m stage's branch by choosing inputs that force it, and row C31 covers the entire
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2^24 input domain, which visits every reachable state of every stage.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C actually branches on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There are **no runtime options, modes, flags, globals, setters, or `#ifdef`s** —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `grep -nE "if *\(|switch|#ifdef|#if |static [^c(]" src` finds no mutable state
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and no conditional compilation. The only axes are input-shape axes:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 1 — `cbRemoveGammaRGB` branch, independently per channel.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `RGB.c > 0.04045` where `RGB.c = byte/255.f`. `10/255 = 0.039216 <= 0.04045`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m and `11/255 = 0.043137 > 0.04045`, so the split is exactly at the byte value:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `L` = linear branch `c / 12.92`  <=> byte in `0..=10`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `P` = `pow((c + 0.055)/1.055, 2.4)` branch  <=> byte in `11..=255`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 2 — `cbApplyGammaRGB` branch, independently per channel.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `x > 0.00313080495356037151702786377709` on the *post-matrix* linear value:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `l` = linear branch `x * 12.92` (this is also the branch every **negative**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   value takes — `pow` is never called with a negative base)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `p` = `1.055 * pow(x, 0.4166666666) - 0.055`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 3 — `cbDenorm` float->`unsigned char` conversion domain**, per channel,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m on `y = x * 255.f + 0.5f`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `in` = `0 <= y < 256` (ordinary truncation)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `neg` = `y < 0` -> `cvttss2si` to `i32` then wrap to 8 bits
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `ovf` = `y >= 256` -> truncate to `i32` then wrap to 8 bits
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Reachability, from the matrix rows in `Tritanopia`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `R' = R + 0.1274*(G - B)` can leave `[0,1]` on **both** sides, so R hits all
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m three of `in`/`neg`/`ovf`. `G'` and `B'` are both `~0.8739*G + 0.1260*B` with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `R` coefficients of `-4.486e-11` / `3.1113e-10`, so they stay in `[0,1]` and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m only ever hit `in`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 4 — argument/return ABI shape.** `cb_rgb_255` is 3 bytes / align 1, so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m under x86-64 SysV it is a single INTEGER-class eightbyte passed and returned in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m one register; the 4th byte is unspecified padding.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## The table
